"smart_blocks:Latin - Semester 1/Latin Written Assessment - Planning.md#3 does not translate '*divisa*' ('divided') - the former two translations translate it correctly in the passive. Likewise, 'parts' seems a better translation than areas (if the intention were areas then '*regio*' would likely have been used to denote a region). One can see how 'comprises' might have been chosen, but if it that was the intended meaning then '*contineo*' or similar might have been used - '*omnis*' is not a synonym": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.06347709,-0.05079329,0.04026442,0.00595083,0.00022784,-0.07878745,-0.00953323,0.06278758,0.00808886,-0.05747852,-0.00669665,-0.12088746,-0.01152273,0.0127113,0.03113461,-0.03638991,-0.06576674,0.00887755,0.02023965,0.00203383,0.12995781,-0.02369567,0.00759427,-0.01841669,0.08262856,0.07957941,0.03082286,0.01044689,-0.02321105,-0.19449796,-0.03582686,0.08488749,-0.01525833,-0.05724043,-0.03260057,0.046814,-0.05518281,0.02468146,-0.05473006,0.04442466,0.01713645,0.033142,0.0072789,-0.0064123,-0.04691768,-0.04341723,-0.06483403,-0.03388698,-0.06683756,0.03407233,0.00911866,-0.01745802,-0.04112566,0.05361535,0.00748853,0.07527051,0.03488461,0.0298116,0.01165644,0.03550891,0.0654111,0.06421535,-0.22605599,0.0505124,-0.04305216,0.01420593,-0.05394144,-0.02043312,-0.01265152,0.11649736,0.01195429,-0.05277105,0.02106164,0.07089235,0.03789173,-0.01703188,0.01607582,-0.00792205,0.01643363,-0.02071644,0.00382826,0.04968691,-0.04163762,-0.00404763,-0.04276412,-0.03859746,-0.00435291,-0.01787718,0.01758773,-0.00621008,0.01297314,-0.11830977,-0.00016659,0.04766132,-0.02066697,-0.0392351,0.00321581,0.02771412,-0.00286904,0.13413861,-0.01077452,0.01678927,0.07232104,-0.00747479,0.00545497,0.00927189,0.03276977,-0.0742484,-0.04100568,0.0134437,-0.03942729,-0.0130474,0.02004008,0.02396363,-0.02551956,-0.03937391,0.10666351,-0.00089737,0.03919591,0.00298037,0.0249567,0.00837032,0.02246623,-0.02055483,0.01344628,-0.00642957,0.0